4. This fork's original code (not from xDrip or Juggluco)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Original to OpenApsAIMI (no upstream provenance marker):
  OnePlusCgmDriver.kt, OnePlusCgmDriverReal.kt, OnePlusCgmDriverStub.kt,
  OnePlusCgmDrivers.kt, OnePlusGlucoseSample.kt, OnePlusGlucoseWatcher.kt,
  OnePlusLogMarkers.kt, OnePlusWarmupState.kt,
  reconnect/OnePlusReconnectPolicy.kt, scan/OnePlusBleScanner.kt,
  scan/OnePlusScanResult.kt, session/OnePlusBackfill.kt,
  session/OnePlusBleSession.kt (reconnect/OEM orchestration; carries
    Juggluco-informed wake-lock / short-auth patterns but is original code),
  session/OnePlusSessionStartPolicy.kt, warmup/OnePlusWarmupClock.kt.
The OEM device-profile abstraction (oem/) and the Android GATT plumbing bulk of
gatt/OnePlusGattClientAndroid.kt are original AAPS implementation; only the
protocol choreography within them is derived (see sections 1 and 2).

Ideas taken from AndroidAPS pull request #5397 (Dexcom G7 direct, author
t1dude), https://github.com/nightscout/AndroidAPS/pull/5397, commit
bec1b16ba20ec646d459a1c724ad41419985b117. That code is AndroidAPS code under the
same AGPL-3 license as this tree; none of its Trio (G7SensorKit, MIT) protocol
code or Trio sounds are used here. Written again on top of this driver, not
copied:
  - OnePlusCommLog.kt (this module): the idea of a 24 hour driver log for the
    log screen (PR file cgm/dexcomg7/core/.../data/G7CommLog.kt). Ours keeps
    the lines in memory only and is fed by the iOS log sink.
  - :plugins:source DexcomOnePlusStatusOverview.kt and DexcomOnePlusLogScreen.kt,
    opened from the plugin tab (DexcomOnePlusComposeContent.kt): the status
    screen and the communication log inside the plugin tab (PR status screen
    and data/G7CommLog.kt).
  - Scanner and session rules (this module): the competing app check and its
    package names (OnePlusCompetingApps.kt), the "slot held" byte of the
    advertisement (OnePlusAdvSlot.kt), stopping before repeated refusals lock
    the sensor (OnePlusAuthRefusals.kt), and keeping a backfill on disconnect
    (OnePlusBackfillSession.kt).
  - :implementation CgmAlarmEngine.kt and the CGM alarm settings: the alarm
    engine of the PR (G7Alarms / G7AlarmEngine), with its two open review
    points fixed. See also implementation/NOTICE.
  - Direct to watch and the watch alarm (:plugins:source
    DexcomOnePlusWatchHandover.kt, :wear): see wear/NOTICE.
  - :plugins:source CameraApplicatorScanner.kt: the applicator Data Matrix scan
    (PR file cgm/dexcomg7/src/.../ui/G7BarcodeScanner.kt), in particular the
    "callback returns true when the code was wanted, then stop" contract. The
    camera code itself follows this fork's own client QR scanner in
    :plugins:sync (QrScanner.android.kt).


